course: dictionary
lesson: 11429
title: Activate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To activate something is to make it start working. «Press the red button to activate the alarm.» The button starts the alarm working, so activate means make it start.
explain: You can activate machines, apps, games and accounts. «Tap the card to activate your new bank account.» When you meet activate in instructions, look at what happens next: the thing begins to work.
explain: In science, to activate a process or chemical is to make it start or become active. «The warm water activated the yeast, and the dough began to rise.» The warm water started the yeast working, so activated means made active.
fact: Activate is a verb. Its forms are activate, activates, activated and activating.
fact: «Activate» means to make something start working.
fact: Instructions often say «Press to activate», which means pressing starts the thing working.
fact: In science, «activate» means to make a process or chemical start or become active, such as warm water activating yeast.
fact: Context clue: if something starts moving, beeping, glowing or working after an action, the word for that action may be activate.
exercise: «Press the red button to activate the alarm.» What does activate mean? | Hide it under the table | Make it stop for ever | Paint it bright red | *Make it start working
exercise: «Tap the card to activate your new bank account.» What is the card for? | Keeping it cold | Cutting paper | Making it start working | *Making it start working, like a bank account being switched on
exercise: «The warm water activated the yeast, and the dough began to rise.» Find and copy the word that means made active. | *activated | rise | dough | warm
test: «Press to activate» is written on a machine. What should you do? | *Press it so the machine starts | Put it in the bin | Turn it upside down | Read it aloud and walk away
test: Ben says activate means to switch off. Why is he wrong? | Activate means to switch off, so Ben is right | Activate means to sleep | Activate means to be quiet | *Activate means to make something start working, the opposite of switching off
exam: Which sentence uses activate correctly? | I activated my lunch and ate it | The sun activated the dark room to sleep | *The new phone needs to be activated before you can use it | The cold rain activated the machine so it stopped
